::  name       receipt refusal field count
::  shape      fields - int (@u32)
::  invariant  a Refusal carries exactly three fields (field - reason -
::             measure)
::  example    3
::  readers    Tally - Mantra - Glow Tend - Sur museum
::  nib        equinox-e208-mantra-tend-v0
::
::  Equinox e208 - Mantra M10 -- tenth Mantra structure pedestal in src/shape/.
::  Names Refusal's field count from tally/receipt_refusal.rye, the record the
::  product contract asks every admission refusal to render: `field` names the
::  contract field that refused, `reason` is the closed Reason set, and
::  `measure` carries value/ceiling/unit exactly when a ceiling decided it.
::  Pedestal only; Rye still owns `render`, the two text refusal readers, and
::  the closed Reason enum this record renders by name.
::
::  Three sits well under rune_shape.max_fields (15); this pedestal does not
::  raise it. Smaller than every receipt or consent fact named so far, because
::  a refusal states what went wrong rather than restating what was offered.
+$  receipt-refusal-field-count-shape
  $:  fields=@u32
  ==
